From: BananaOS Duo Lite bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: initialize CRTC state before releasing mixers

ROCKNIX resource-cleanup patch writes num_mixers before assigning cstate.
Initialize the pointer at declaration. The alpha1 device log faults at
dpu_crtc_atomic_check+0x320, mapped to this exact write via faddr2line.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -1438,7 +1438,7 @@
 	int i, num_lm, num_ctl, num_dspp;
 	struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms = _dpu_crtc_get_kms(crtc);
 	struct dpu_global_state *global_state;
-	struct dpu_crtc_state *cstate;
+	struct dpu_crtc_state *cstate = to_dpu_crtc_state(crtc_state);
 	struct msm_display_topology topology;
 	int ret;
 
